SUMMARY:Hidden Mythologies: Karelian Traditions & Myths
DESCRIPTION:Event Details:  Now in its second year\, the Hidden Mythologi
 eslecture series explores the rich and often overlooked mythological trad
 itions of the peoples of the Volga-Ural region and beyond. Through storie
 s of gods\, spirits\, legendary heroes\, sacred landscapes\, and traditio
 nal beliefs\, the series examines the ways mythology reflects and preserv
 es the cultures and worldviews of diverse communities across Eurasia.  Jo
 urney into the forests and mythological traditions of the Karelian people
 \, exploring the Meteliläinens and the celebrated Finnish-Karelian epic\
 , the Kalevala. Discover a world in which the forest\, poetry\, magic\, a
 nd mythology are deeply intertwined. The program features traditional Kar
 elian ballads\, including Vellamon Neidon Onginta\, Kanteleen Synty\, and
  Loitsu Saunassa. The program concludes with a live performance of the Ka
 relia folk song Kukkuu - Kukkuu.  Each program begins with a presentation
  by Dr. Golshat Safiullina exploring an aspect of the featured culture's 
 mythological traditions\, followed by Folk Song Club\, an interactive mus
 ical experience curated by musical director Daryana Antipova\, bringing a
 nother dimension to the stories\, beliefs\, and cultural heritage explore
 d in the lecture.  This event is held in collaboration with the Slavic an
 d East European Languages Department\, the Jacobs School of Music\, and t
 he CHAKCHAK: Languages and Cultures Foundation.Parking Information:  Limi
 ted complimentary parking is available in front of the Museum entrance (h
 ttps://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA) off Indiana Avenue. Street park
 ing is free on weekends and weekdays after 5:00 PM in the neighborhoods s
 urrounding the Museum. Paid parking options include the University Collec
 tions at McCalla (https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcjDeCACruHA) parking lot 
 off Indiana Avenue\, the Indiana Memorial Union (https://maps.app.goo.gl/
 2n49VoLuF78o5twJA) visitor lot\, and nearby metered street parking.  Conv
 enient metered street parking is available in the downtown/Sample Gates a
 rea along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4th Street\, North Lin
 coln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant Street.Questions?  For 
 accessibility assistance or questions about this event\, please reach out
  to Camden Hill at camrhill@iu.edu (mailto:camrhill@iu.edu) or (812) 855-
 1696.Note:  By attending this event\, you agree to be in photography that
  may be used by the University for promotional purposes. If you would not
  like to be in any pictures\, please speak to a Museum staff member and t
 hey will inform assigned photographers of your request. If you see that y
 our image has been used in error\, please reach out to iumaa@iu.edu (mail
 to:iumaa@iu.edu) to request that it be taken down.
