SUMMARY:Winter at the Museum
DESCRIPTION:Event Details:&#160\;  Get out of the cold and cozy up for a 
 night of winter wonder! Join the IUMAA for Winter at the Museum\, a festi
 ve evening filled with a flurry of creativity and imagination.Decorate a 
 wreath\, candle holder\, and dreidel while surrounded by delicate harp me
 lodies.  Thinking of loved ones far away? Decorate your own holiday card 
 to send their way!  Want to add some flair to your own home festivities? 
 Make some beaded garlands and decorate your own ornaments.    Don't forge
 t to enjoy some hot chocolate and holiday pastries!  This program is free
  and open to all\, with Museum galleries remaining open for the duration 
 of the event to give a special\, after-hours view of the exhibitions.Park
 ing Information:  Limited complimentary parking is available in front of 
 the Museum entrance (https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA) off India
 na Avenue. Free street parking is available in surrounding neighborhoods 
 on weekends and weekdays after 5:00 PM.  Paid parking is also available i
 n the University Collections at McCalla (https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcj
 DeCACruHA) parking lot off Indiana Avenue and the Indiana Memorial Union 
 (https://maps.app.goo.gl/2n49VoLuF78o5twJA) visitor lot.  Metered street 
 parking is also available near Sample Gates and throughout downtown Bloom
 ington\, including along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4th Str
 eet\, North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant Street.Q
 uestions?  For accessibility assistance or questions about this event\, p
 lease reach out to Camden Hill at camrhill@iu.edu (mailto:camrhill@iu.edu
 ) or (812) 855-1696.Note:  By attending this event\, you agree to be in p
 hotography that may be used by the University for promotional purposes. I
 f you would not like to be in any pictures\, please speak to a Museum sta
 ff member and they will inform assigned photographers of your request. If
  you see that your image has been used in error\, please reach out to ium
 aa@iu.edu (mailto:iumaa@iu.edu) to request that it be taken down.
